    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "1// Check whether a student passed or failed the exam.\n2// We will assume the passing score is 50 or above.\n3\n4#include <stdio.h>\n5\n6int main() {\n7\n8    int score;\n9  \n10    // Get student score from the user\n11    printf(\"Enter score: \");\n12    scanf(\"%d\", &score);\n13\n14    // Print pass message if score is 50 or above\n15    if (score >= 50) {\n16        printf(\"Congratulations!\\n\");\n17        printf(\"You passed the examination.\");\n18    }\n19  \n20    return 0;\n21}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sample Output 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Enter score: 72\nCongratulations!\nYou passed the examination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the user enters 72, score >= 50 in the if statement will be 1 (true). In this case, the statements inside the if statement are executed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sample Output 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Enter score: 42"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the user enters 35, score >= 50 in the if statement will be 0 (false). In this case, the statements inside the if statement are skipped from execution."
    },
